WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.050
<v Instructor>So now let's have a look at AWS DMS.</v>

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.000
So you click on get started,

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.590
and this gives you just an overview page

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.690
of what you can do with DMS,

5
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.730
but the real magic happens on the left-hand side.

6
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.700
So this can change, but the idea remains the same.

7
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.070
You can do a discovery and assessment

8
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.200
in which you're going to create a data collector,

9
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.120
find databases, analyze inventory,

10
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.860
and then use the recommendations.

11
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.560
You can convert or move to managed,

12
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.480
so the idea is that you convert a schema

13
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.060
using the DMS Schema Conversion tool.

14
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.910
Then you move your data into AWS

15
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.620
and you move to a managed service,

16
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.170
or you can migrate or replicate data.

17
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.870
And here, we choose the end points,

18
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.220
we're gonna see this in a second.

19
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.390
We create a provision instance

20
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.550
and we create a task for the replication.

21
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.470
You see that for some of these options,

22
00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.540
we have Provisioned or Serverless

23
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.910
for the migration of the replication.

24
00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.700
And here to convert a database,

25
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.900
we have this schema conversion.

26
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.090
Or if we don't convert the schema,

27
00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.700
we have a homogeneous data migration.

28
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.460
So this is just to give you an overview of DMS,

29
00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.350
but the real magic happens on left-hand side.

30
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:08.100
So here you're going to go into Endpoints

31
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.030
and we're going to look at it.

32
00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:13.140
So first of all, this is how to move data.

33
00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.660
So it could be from source to target,

34
00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.520
and so you must create an endpoint

35
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.920
for the source and the target.

36
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.830
So the idea is that I will create an endpoint,

37
00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.570
and here you choose whatever you want.

38
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.760
So you enter an identifier,

39
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.620
and then you have to choose the source engine.

40
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.680
So you have all these options for the source engines.

41
00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.500
For example, you choose Amazon Aurora MySQL.

42
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.580
And then you have to enter

43
00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.470
all the information about the endpoint.

44
00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.340
We cannot do this

45
00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.530
because we don't have an Aurora database ready,

46
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.850
but you get the idea.

47
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.250
Finally, you have the option for some databases

48
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.200
to test the endpoint connection.

49
00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.570
This is optional, but at least you're able to see

50
00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.970
whether or not your replication instance,

51
00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.170
that we'll create in a second,

52
00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.420
can connect to your source.

53
00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.150
So you have the same type of idea with target

54
00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.780
in which you say what you want DMS to write to.

55
00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.480
And again, you need to choose a target engine

56
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.650
amongst the list.

57
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:05.940
And you enter some configuration.

58
00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.730
For example, if you choose DynamoDB right here,

59
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.940
you enter a service role access, endpoint setting,

60
00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.170
wizard, editor, and so on,

61
00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.320
and then test again the connection to the endpoint.

62
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.300
So you get a lot of information as well

63
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.920
when you choose an endpoint on the right-hand side

64
00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.590
around what to do and the best practices.

65
00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.110
So once you've created two endpoints,

66
00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.450
you can create a replication task.

67
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.310
And so you have two options.

68
00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.870
For this task, you can either create

69
00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.820
a replication instance,

70
00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.380
and here you create a replication instance

71
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.870
by actually creating a physical server.

72
00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.420
So here, we can choose the size of the server,

73
00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.320
as you can see.

74
00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.580
For the bigger replication task,

75
00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.530
you may want to choose a bigger server.

76
00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.570
And you can click here to estimate

77
00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.250
the instance class and storage.

78
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.630
And then you can configure it.

79
00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.090
You say whether or not you want high availability,

80
00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.410
the networking type,

81
00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.180
you apply a subnet group,

82
00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.850
you will apply security groups and so on,

83
00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.170
and then you have an instance.

84
00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:01.470
Or optionally, you can use serverless.

85
00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.150
And so if it's serverless,

86
00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:06.480
then you don't need to provision an instance.

87
00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.280
So here, when you go to Provisioned instances,

88
00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.920
it's not to do serverless, it's to do the opposites.

89
00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.020
So when you go to tasks, here we go,

90
00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.060
you can create a task,

91
00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.150
and you're going to specify the source database endpoint

92
00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:19.860
that we've created from before,

93
00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.920
the target database endpoint that we've created after,

94
00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:23.820
and then the task mode.

95
00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.170
So if it's provisioned,

96
00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.030
we need to select the provisioned instance

97
00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.740
that we'll have created from before,

98
00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.030
or if it's serverless,

99
00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.580
then DMS will automatically adjust

100
00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.630
the level of compute needed

101
00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.340
for your migration error application task,

102
00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.270
and we don't need to select the type of instance we need.

103
00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.570
So this is an easier option, I would say.

104
00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.590
Now you choose the test types.

105
00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.810
So you want to migrate data once,

106
00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.520
do you want to migrate and replicate?

107
00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.630
Which means a full load

108
00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:51.300
and then anytime the source data changes,

109
00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.950
you're going to replicate these changes,

110
00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.390
it's called CDC.

111
00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.580
Or do you want to just do the replication?

112
00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.050
And then for how long?

113
00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.490
And then once you've done that,

114
00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.680
based on what your source and your target is,

115
00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.530
you can specify some settings and so on

116
00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.250
for some logging, some connectivity,

117
00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.560
how to do it, so it's quite a complete service.

118
00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.530
To go deep into setting a replication, it takes time.

119
00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.850
But from this overview,

120
00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.520
what I want to show you is that you have the idea

121
00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.540
behind all the steps needed to set up DMS

122
00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.520
and migrate a database

123
00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.340
from one source engine to a target engine,

124
00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.540
and with two options,

125
00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:30.000
serverless or provisioned instances.

126
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.930
So that's it for this lecture,

127
00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:31.950
I hope you liked it,

128
00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.023
and I will see you in the next lecture.

